gs memoryview() and bytes() ask a __buffer__ for."] [365 1 "// bufferOf is a class's __buffer__(flags): its memoryview, nil when the type has none (PY7: memoryview() and bytes()"] [366 1 "// of such an object raised TypeError)."] [382 1 "// releaseBuffer is PyBuffer_Release of a view bufferOf got: the exporter's __release_buffer__(view), when it has one."] [391 1 "// release is memoryview.release(): the exporter's buffer released once."] [413 1 "// mvItemSizes are get_native_fmtchar's formats and their native sizes (64-bit Linux; queue 263: n N f d e ? P too)."] [417 1 "// mvFmtChar is a native single-character format without its optional '@' (get_native_fmtchar's character)."] [425 1 "// mvFmtSize is get_native_fmtchar: a native format's item size, false when f is none (3.15.2: also \"Zf\" and \"Zd\","] [426 1 "// the complex formats; 3.14.10: one character only)."] [441 1 "// mvByteFmt is IS_BYTE_FORMAT of a view's format: 'b', 'B' or 'c', with an optional '@'."] [458 1 "// item is the i-th item of a cast view: little-endian, signed for the lower-case formats."] [463 54 "// queue 263: unpack_single's other native formats, as the struct module's"] [464 31 "// 3.15.2's complexes: the struct module's F and D, native"] [505 1 "// BytesLike makes a memoryview a bytes-like object (asBytes): a copy of its bytes."] [519 4 "// a view of a view: the same buffer, start, length and stride (CPython's memory_from_buffer keeps the"] [520 4 "// strides, so a non-contiguous view stays one)"] [527 42 "// picklebuf_getbuf: the object's own buffer"] [541 4 "// the export of a class's __buffer__: its __release_buffer__ called when the last view goes"] [550 40 "// queue 260: the exporter's format, itemsize and shape"] [556 2 "// memory_hash (queue 249): a read-only byte view's hash is its bytes' (hash(b'..')), the exporter hashed first with"] [557 2 "// the view exported meanwhile (gh-142664: a re-entrant __hash__ that releases the view gets BufferError)"] [638 2 "// item and slice assignment into a writable buffer (PY6d's REQUEST: _pyio's readinto, pickle's protocol 5"] [639 2 "// bytearray); byte views only"] [652 17 "// queue 260: a shaped view's items are the struct module's formats (memory_ass_sub's adjust_fmt)"] [664 27 "// queue 263: a 0-dim view's one item (a cast to shape ())"] [732 3 "// queue 260 (memory_richcompare): views of other shapes differ (equiv_shape), and a format the struct module"] [733 3 "// cannot unpack (\"T{...}\", \"&<i\", \"<O\") makes the views unequal, a view itself included"] [768 17 "// queue 260: tolist_rec over the exporter's shape, native formats only (adjust_fmt)"] [789 2 "// cast (queue 263): memoryview_cast_impl over cast_to_1D and cast_to_ND, Objects/memoryobject.c (3.14.10): the"] [790 2 "// format, then a shape of any number of dimensions (1D -> ND or ND -> 1D); the result a view of the same memory"] [810 74 "// MV_C_CONTIGUOUS"] [838 3 "// cast_to_1D"] [851 18 "// not a native single character: not a byte format"] [860 3 "// a strided view of at most one item is C-contiguous: the cast's view starts at its item, step 1"] [862 21 "// cast_to_ND: copy_shape, then the buffer's size"] [898 2 "// count, index and toreadonly (PY7: absent): over tolist's items, as memory_count and memory_index"] [910 81 "// queue 263: memory_iter's checks"] [936 81 "// queue 263: memoryview_index_impl's"] [980 3 "// a 1-D view's shape, strides and contiguity (PY7: absent)"] [992 18 "// C-contiguous: init_strides_from_shape"] [1021 34 "// CHECK_RELEASED (PY7: obj stayed readable; no attribute \"released\", CPython's has none)"] [1029 1 "// unusable is the view's CHECK_RELEASED, and its exporter's own check when it has one (queue 204: an mmap closed under"] [1030 1 "// the view raises ValueError \"mmap closed or invalid\", where CPython's mmap refuses the close; pyi counts no exports)."] [1041 1 "// isReadonly is view->readonly: a toreadonly's or __buffer__'s view, or one of an exporter that is not writable (queue 249:"] [1042 1 "